From 79ffdd6aae0dd1b4bc9ee26cf3d4b409f765825a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 21:20:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: P25T: enable i2c1 to identify
 accelerometer chip

The stock Android DT lists two alternative accelerometers on i2c1,
both left status = "okay" (unlike the four vdd_cpu regulator
alternatives on i2c0, where only one is actually populated):

  - sensor@19    "gs_sc7a20"  0x19
  - sensorda@27  "gs_da223"   0x27

Since both are marked okay in the stock DT, Android appears to probe
both at runtime and let whichever chip actually answers win. We don't
yet have a child node for either one - this patch only enables the
i2c1 bus itself so a follow-up i2cdetect/i2cget diagnostic can find
out, on real hardware, which chip is physically present:

  - SC7A20 register-maps like the ST LIS3DH/LIS2DH12 family, which has
    a mainline driver (st_accel). However st_sensors_core.c gates on
    an exact WHOAMI/WAI register match before it will bind - even a
    register-compatible clone chip is refused if the WHOAMI byte
    doesn't match, so this is only "close" if that byte also matches.
  - DA223 has no mainline driver of any kind at present; supporting it
    would mean writing one from scratch.

No accelerometer child node is added here - this is a read-only
discovery step, same spirit as how RK817 was first probed on i2c0
before any regulator work went in. i2c1 also feeds the touchscreen
(Silead GSL3673 @0x40, separate TODO), so enabling the bus benefits
that item too.

Also fixes a now-stale comment above &i2c0 that still described the
SYR837 vdd_cpu regulator as "no node, read-only probing only" - no
longer accurate since patch 0011 added the real vdd_cpu node. Updated
to correctly reference patches 0008-0009 and 0011.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0156c5MfQpFxaYWNNLMrcym9
---
 .../boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-teclast-p25t.dts | 31 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-teclast-p25t.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-teclast-p25t.dts
index c034f062b..f8194ed90 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-teclast-p25t.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-teclast-p25t.dts
@@ -332,11 +332,12 @@ &pwm14 {
 };
 
 /*
- * I2C0: RK817 PMIC @0x20, SYR837 @0x40 (SYR837 still has no node, read-only
- * probing only). The RK817 node below is deliberately minimal: only the
- * two regulators needed to power the USB-C port's VBUS, nothing else on
- * the chip (no battery/codec/pwrkey/RTC). Values copied verbatim from the
- * stock Android device tree (Firmware/dt/boot-0-0x6c0fe00.dts):
+ * I2C0: RK817 PMIC @0x20 (BOOST/OTG_SWITCH regulators + charger/battery,
+ * patches 0008-0009) and SYR837 @0x40 (vdd_cpu, patch 0011). The RK817
+ * node itself stays deliberately minimal beyond that (no codec/pwrkey
+ * node - both came up for free once the chip had any node at all).
+ * Values copied verbatim from the stock Android device tree
+ * (Firmware/dt/boot-0-0x6c0fe00.dts):
  *   - BOOST: regulator-always-on there too - stock never turns this rail
  *     off, we are not switching on anything stock treats as off.
  *   - OTG_SWITCH: stock leaves it switchable (its own USB HAL enables it
@@ -434,3 +435,23 @@ &cpu2 {
 &cpu3 {
 	cpu-supply = <&vdd_cpu>;
 };
+
+/*
+ * I2C1: bus enable only, no chip node yet. Investigation step: the stock
+ * DT lists TWO alternative accelerometers here, both marked status="okay"
+ * unlike vdd_cpu's four alternatives (only one of which was real) - so
+ * Android probes both and whichever chip actually answers wins:
+ *   - sensor@19  "gs_sc7a20"  0x19 - has a mainline-compatible register
+ *     map (ST LIS3DH/LIS2DH12 family) IF its WHOAMI byte matches; if so,
+ *     just a DT node away.
+ *   - sensorda@27 "gs_da223"  0x27 - no mainline driver at all for this
+ *     chip; would need one written from scratch.
+ * Enabling the bus lets us i2cdetect/i2cget which one is really here
+ * before deciding which path applies. No child node added - purely
+ * read-only discovery, same spirit as how RK817 was first probed on
+ * i2c0 before any regulator work. Also feeds the touchscreen (Silead
+ * GSL3673 @0x40, separate TODO).
+ */
+&i2c1 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
